<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you create an account, we store your email address, a hashed password (or, if you sign in with Google/GitHub, your provider's account ID — never a password), your JC balance, and basic deployment history (which bot, when, and its status).</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>2. What we don't store</h2>
  <p>Your WhatsApp session string and any other bot configuration values you enter on the deploy form are sent directly to our infrastructure provider to run your bot — we don't save them in our own database. If you lose access to a deployed bot's session, you'll need to re-pair it.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use a single session cookie to keep you logged in. It doesn't track you across other sites and isn't used for advertising.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>4. Third parties we use</h2>
  <ul class="legal-list">
    <li>A database provider, to store account and deployment records</li>
    <li>An infrastructure provider, to build and run deployed bots</li>
    <li>An email provider, to send verification codes</li>
    <li>Google and/or GitHub, if you choose to sign in with either — we only receive your email address and account ID, nothing else from your profile</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>5. Referrals</h2>
  <p>If someone signs up using your referral link, we record the connection between your accounts so we can credit the referral bonus. We don't share either party's email with the other.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>6. Your data, your choices</h2>
  <p>You can request a copy of the data we hold on your account, or ask us to delete your account and associated data, by emailing us. We'll action deletion requests within a reasonable time, except where we need to retain records for fraud prevention or legal reasons.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes materially, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
</section>

<section class="legal-section">
  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about your data: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a></p>
</section>
